30	    protected MembershipLevelEvaluator membershipLevelEvaluator;
44	    @Mapping(target = "membershipLevel", expression = "java(membershipLevelEvaluator.levelFor(owner))")
```

## 2. Owner entity

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`**. It is `@Entity @Table(name = "owners")` and `extends Person` (which extends `BaseEntity`). Relevant fields (lines 39-81):

- `email` (line 52-54): `@Column(name="email") @Email private String email;` — with helper `hasEmail()` (lines 118-120): `return this.email != null && !this.email.isBlank();`
- `namesakeCount` (lines 71-72): `@Column(name="namesake_count") private Integer namesakeCount;` — getter/setter lines 162-168.
- `householdId` (lines 68-69): `@Column(name="household_id") private String householdId;` — getter/setter lines 154-160. (Note: it's `householdId`, a String, not a `household` object.)
- `registrationDate` (lines 62-63): `@Column(name="registration_date") private LocalDate registrationDate;`
- `birthDate` (lines 65-66): `@Column(name="birth_date") private LocalDate birthDate;`
- Other fields: `address`, `city`, `telephone`, `postcode`, `customerCode`, `possibleDuplicate`, `possibleDuplicateOf`, and `Set<Pet> pets`.

Inherited: `firstName`, `lastName` (from `Person`), `id` (from `BaseEntity`).

**There is NO `tenure` field and NO `createdAt`/creation-date field anywhere on the entity.** The only date fields are `registrationDate` and `birthDate`. `BaseEntity` (`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/BaseEntity.java`) has only `id`; `Person` (`.../model/Person.java`) has only `firstName`/`lastName` — neither carries any timestamp/auditing fields.

## 3. Tests related to membership level

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java`** (full contents):
```java
7	/** tenure-cap: level 4 requires tenure over 365 days, so a brand-new owner (zero tenure)
8	 * never exceeds level 3. A new owner with an email and no namesake maxes the pre-tenure factors,
9	 * and must land at level 3, not 4. */
10	class AcceptanceTest extends AcceptanceBase {
12		@Test
13		void coreNewOwnerCappedAtLevel3() throws Exception {
14			ObjectNode o = withPostcode(ownerNode());
15			o.put("email", uniqueEmail());
16			int id = createOwnerOk(o);
17			getOwner(id).andExpect(jsonPath("$.membershipLevel").value(3));
18		}
19	}
```
This is a black-box acceptance test: it POSTs `/api/owners` with an email (and a unique name, so `namesakeCount` is 0) and asserts `$.membershipLevel == 3`. Its base class is `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceBase.java` (helpers only — `ownerNode()`, `withPostcode()`, `uniqueEmail()`, `createOwnerOk()`, `getOwner()`, etc.; no membership logic). No unit test exists for `MembershipLevelEvaluator` directly.

## 4. How tenure is currently defined/computed

**Tenure is not defined or computed anywhere.** It exists only as intent expressed in comments/tests:

- `MembershipLevelEvaluator` javadoc (lines 29, 37): "The result is capped at MAX_LEVEL; level 4 is reserved for tenure."
- `AcceptanceTest` comment (lines 7-9): "level 4 requires tenure over 365 days, so a brand-new owner (zero tenure) never exceeds level 3."

There is no `tenure` field, getter, or method in the codebase, and no code reads any creation/registration date to derive elapsed time. The evaluator hard-caps at 3, so level 4 is currently unreachable. If tenure were to be implemented, note there is **no `createdAt` timestamp** — the closest existing candidate is `Owner.registrationDate` (`LocalDate`), and today's date is fixed in context as 2026-09-20.

**Namesake counting** (feeds the level computation) lives in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/NamesakeCounter.java`: `count()` (lines 38-45) counts existing owners matching the candidate's first+last name case-insensitively; that value is stored on `Owner.namesakeCount`.

